.TH SINDOOK-PATHS 1 "2026-08-15" "sindook 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sindook-paths \- show the portable Sindook configuration locations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sindook paths
[\fB\-json\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the operating-system-specific directory used for Sindook's
public contacts and default identity path, along with the state of
the default identity. \fBSINDOOK_CONFIG_DIR\fP overrides the location
for a portable install or an isolated automation run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-json\fP
machine-readable output: one JSON object
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sindook (1),
.BR sindook-init (1),
.BR sindook-contacts (1)
